  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "note_56",
      "text": "Models a binary outcome (yIN) from one or more predictors (xIN) by iteratively-reweighted least squares. The outcome may be numeric 0/1 or a two-level category (the second level, alphabetically, is taken as the positive class = 1). Reports one row per term: the coefficient (log-odds), standard error, Wald z and p-value, odds ratio and its 95% confidence interval, plus the model log-likelihood, likelihood-ratio test against the null and McFadden pseudo-R². It warns on non-convergence, which usually signals separation (a predictor splits the outcome cleanly). Estimates match statsmodels. Alongside the coefficient table it emits three per-observation columns, outcome, eta (the linear predictor Xβ) and fitted (the predicted probability), so the quick-plot draws fitted probability against the linear predictor (the S-curve, for any number of predictors) with the observed 0/1 outcomes overlaid, and you can rebuild that plot by hand from the columns. Cox 1958.",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 24,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 190
    }
  ],
